      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A report is given on the results achieved in the palliative treatment of bone metastases by means of conventional radiotherapy in fifty unselected patients with different types of primary tumours. 14 % showed and excellent response and in 56 % a good result was obtained. In 14 % of the patients the treatment was unsuccessful, while in 16 % it was not possible to complete therapy because of the poor general condition of the patients. The response was independent of the histology or localization of the primary tumour."},
